//! Byte signatures for the radio-bypass targets.
//!
//! Generated by `cargo run -p flashimg --example derive-signature`, from
//! `PURR-OS-ESP32/CoreOS/build_tdeck_plus` (ESP-IDF v5.3.5, ESP32-S3). The
//! masks are not stored: [`Signature::from_xtensa`] recomputes them from the
//! code, so the rule and the data cannot drift apart.
//!
//! These are the raw function bodies. They are specific to a compilation --
//! a different IDF version or a different sdkconfig produces different code,
//! and the same function is 138 bytes in some ESP32-S3 builds and 154 here.
//! When a signature stops matching, that is what has happened, and the fix is
//! to derive a new one from a build that does have symbols rather than to
//! loosen the mask.
//!
//! `esp_wifi_connect` and `esp_wifi_disconnect` are deliberately absent. Both
//! compile to ten bytes -- a stack frame, one call, a return -- which matched
//! six places in the same image. A signature that cannot tell a function from
//! five others is not a signature, and guessing between them would patch the
//! wrong code.

